        // Let's assert that marketDrugs is exactly 1000 + (drugsBought / 10)
        // But we don't know drugsBought from outside...

        // Simpler approach: after collect, marketDrugs in reference is seedMarket + (drugsBuilt/10)
        // In bug it's seedMarket + (drugsBuilt/5). Both are positive. The bug's value is larger.
        // We can set an upper bound that reference passes but bug fails.

        // Compute drugBought roughly: eth = 1 ether, balance before = 0
        // calculateDrugBuy(1 ether, 1 ether, 1000) returns a value
        // We can use the public view to compute expected drugsBought
        uint256 drugsBought = c.calculateDrugBuySimple(1 ether);
        uint256 expectedMarketAdd = drugsBought / 10; // fee already subtracted
        // But fee subtraction happens before adding to market...
        // Actually the fee is subtracted from drugsBought before adding to claimedDrugs
        // The marketDrugs addition uses the full drugsUsed (which includes claimedDrugs + time-based)

        // Let me simplify: after collect with no referral check complications,
        // The marketDrugs in reference will be 1000 + (drugsUsed / 10)
        // and in bug it's 1000 + (drugsUsed / 5)
        // Since drugsUsed > 0, the bug adds more.

